  "question": {
    "text": "The tangent at point \\((a \\cos \\theta, b \\sin \\theta), 0  < \\theta < \\frac{\\pi}{2}\\), to the ellipse \\(\\frac{x^2}{a^2}+\\frac{y^2}{b^2}=1\\) meets the \\(x\\)-axis at \\(T\\) and \\(y\\)-axis at \\(T_1\\). Then the value of \\(\\min _{0 < \\theta < \\frac{\\pi}{2}}(O T)\\left(O T_1\\right)\\) is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\\(a b\\)",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\\(2 \\mathrm{ab}\\)",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "0",
      "is_correct": false
